---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  section="about"
  description="Kyle James Walker is a Distinguished Data Engineer at Zefr and helps organize Data Con LA."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="display text-3xl sm:text-4xl">About</h1>

    <div class="prose-kjw mt-6">
      <p>
        I am Kyle James Walker. I work at Zefr as a Distinguished Data
        Engineer, and a partner and organizer of Data Con LA. This website contains a
        collection of some of my open source projects.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of these exist because there either wasn't a tool that matched
        what I wanted, or it was a fun way to expand one of my hobbies, or I
        just wanted to see how much work it would take to build. The presenting
        tools were built for Data Con LA, or came out of running the
        conference.
      </p>

      <h2>How the things here work</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/apps/">apps</a> run entirely in your browser. There is no
        account, no upload and no server doing the work. Close the tab and
        nothing of yours is left anywhere but your own machine.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/projects/">projects</a> are on GitHub under the MIT
        license.
      </p>

      <h2>This site</h2>
      <p>
        Built with Astro and Tailwind, deployed to GitHub Pages. Every app in
        it is a self-contained project: copy its directory out of the
        repository, run <code>npm install &amp;&amp; npm run dev</code>, and it
        works with nothing of this site attached. That is enforced in CI, not
        just intended.
      </p>
      <p>
        The photograph in the header is a stack of sugar cubes, lit from three
        sides. I took it in 2015.
      </p>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={site.links.github} rel="me noopener">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href={site.links.linkedin} rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li><a href={site.links.email}>Email</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
